**Every cell is inside the 25 % goal, and only the inter arm is above 1.0x at
all** — 1.035x to 1.122x against C, where the same grid on `main` reads 1.279x
to 1.334x. Of that improvement the encoder change (`mecand`) is 2.0-8.2 % and
this harness change is the rest.

=================== HOW TO READ THE RATIO NOW =================================

The port and C harnesses now hold the same one copy of the sequence, so the
`harn/C` columns are a comparison of encoders. If you want the encoders alone,
subtract 12.58 M (2 frames at 4 MP) from both sides.

The inter arm's C `.obu` is NOT byte-identical to the port's at these sizes
(148,295 vs 139,762 at 2048x2048 — the inter byte frontier is 64/128/256
square), so those cells compare two encoders doing SIMILAR, not identical,
work. The still and videokey arms ARE byte-identical at every size here.

=================== NOT ESTABLISHED ===========================================
  * Any aarch64 number. x86_64-linux only; different allocator and page size.
  * Any preset but 13, content but gradient, qp but 40, size outside 1280-2048.
  * Repeat variance on the heap half: one encode per cell.
  * That `tools/mem_gate.sh`'s recorded ratios move by the same amounts — that
    gate measures `tools/identity_run` by default, which is a DIFFERENT harness
    with its own overhead (measured at ~14.5 MiB more than the encoder at 4 MP,
    benchmarks/mem_2026-09-02.meta) and is not touched here.
